  "query_preview": "..\n(Tomorrow through Friday)\nIssued at 1237 PM CDT Fri Aug 7 2026\n\nShower/storm chances linger across parts of southeast Oklahoma\ninto western Arkansas during the day Saturday before the remnants\nof the surface boundaries and the compact area of low pressure\nexit. Behind/north of the precip chances, cloud cover is forecast\nto become more scattered allowing for hot/humid conditions to\nspread over much of the CWA. Forecast high temperatures again in\nthe mid 90s to around 100 deg are anticipated along with heat \nindex values of 100 to 108 deg. Have issued a Heat Advisory for\nmuch of eastern Oklahoma and also the Arkansas River valley of\nwest central Arkansas from Noon to 8 PM. Conditions in west\ncentral Arkansas could be impacted from the low precip chances \ndepending on how long it lingers. Have also kept far southeast\nOklahoma out of the advisory due to the precip chances. Shower and\nstorm chances finally exit the CWA by Saturday evening.\n\nHigh pressure centered out west is progged to expand eastward into\nthe southern Plains Sunday and remain through the first half of\nnext week. In response. the ongoing heat and humidity are forecast\nto remain common for the CWA through the middle of next week.\nThus, afternoon temperatures of upper 90s to around 102 deg are\nforecast for most locations, and combined with heat index values\nof 100 to 109 deg will create likely heat headlines each day for\nmuch of the CWA. There are some indications for the latter part of\nnext week for the ridge to retreat westward with a shortwave\ndropping through the Plains. If this trend conditions, then \nprecip chances could return toward the end of the forecast period.",
